+  // windows in tiles follow it, keeping their tile's share of the work area
+  // (a tile is stored relative to the work area it was made in), eased like
+  // any tiling move. Floating windows are left alone; maximized windows are
+  // re-fitted by Mutter itself.
+  //
+  // Only once the layout has settled: the reflow waits until the work area
+  // has not changed for LUMA_REFLOW_SETTLE ms and window memory is not
+  // putting windows back (after a resume or a monitor change), moves each
+  // window at most once per settled work area, never to another monitor,
+  // and stops moving a window that was moved more than LUMA_REFLOW_BURST
+  // times in LUMA_REFLOW_WINDOW ms (logged for Vitals).
